 "notes": "audit_1: TK724 (6 5/16) and TK727 (8 app) have only room-scene photos, which the photo picker accepted and traced into solid slabs. 6 5/16 uses photo 99 (none) so it borrows the 5 1/16 silhouette. 8 app is the 12 in app outline re-lengthened by hand (posts moved onto the 8 in c2c, the bar between them scaled uniformly, Y to the 1 3/4 in projection), because the generator's borrow squeezed the bar's swell into the middle third. Bevels lowered per size to the largest value whose inset caps do not fold into webs across the gap (the swelling bar is thin at its ends and feet)."
